/*
updateContentCommand
--------------------

The second of three lifecycle hooks (`initCommand`, `updateContentCommand`,
`postCreateCommand`) used to finish setting up a dev-container.

• Runs **inside** the container **after** `onCreateCommand` whenever new files
  appear in the workspace during creation.
• Executes at least once; cloud providers may run it again to refresh cached
  or pre-built containers.
• Only repository- or organisation-scoped secrets are available—assume no
  user-scoped credentials.
• Array form is executed directly (no shell).

---

**Viewing the output**

In the JetBrains client IDE choose **Help ▸ Collect Host and Client Logs**.
Unzip the archive and open `Host/idea.log` to see the command’s terminal
output.
*/

{
  "name": "spec-lifecycle_updateContentCommand",
  "image": "ubuntu:latest",
  //  "updateContentCommand": "echo 'Initializing Dev Container...'"
  //  "updateContentCommand": ["sh", "-c", "echo 'Initializing Dev Container...'"]
  "updateContentCommand": {
    "1": "ls /",
    "2": "echo 'UpdateContentCommand...'",
    "3": "echo 'ok'"
  }
}
